        "original_id": "3d4af00e-3a82-5407-bae2-695f84c4c256",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Laws: Lex Antonia\n- Offices and concepts: Dictatorship, final decree of the Senate\n- People: Lucius Cornelius Sulla Felix, Caesar\n- Roles: Roman general, statesman\n\nFacts:\n- Lucius Cornelius Sulla Felix, commonly known as Sulla, lived circa 138 BC to 78 BC.\n- Lucius Cornelius Sulla Felix was a Roman general and statesman.\n- Lex Antonia formally abolished the Dictatorship.\n- Lex Antonia was the second law to abolish the Dictatorship.\n- The first law abolishing the Dictatorship was passed after the Second Punic War and replaced the Dictatorship with the final decree of the Senate.\n- The earlier law was effectively nullified by the later Dictatorships of Sulla and Caesar.",
